    "content": "From: Helena Vosloo <helena.vosloo@meridianbank.example>\nTo: Priya Raghavan <p.raghavan@northgate-advisory.example>\nCc: Daniel Okafor, Kenji Mori, Programme Mailbox\nDate: Friday 19 June 2026, 17:42\nSubject: RE: Onboarding platform - cost envelope for discovery\n\nPriya,\n\nFollowing the capital committee on Wednesday, I can now give you the envelope\nyou asked for in week one.\n\nInfrastructure spend for the onboarding platform must not exceed $200,000 in the\nfirst twelve months of operation. That figure covers compute, storage, network\nand the private cloud tenancy uplift. It does not cover the screening vendor\nlicence, which sits in the financial crime cost centre, and it does not cover\nNorthgate's fees.\n\nAny spend above that threshold requires a separate capital request, which in\npractice means the November committee at the earliest and a three to four month\ndelay. I would strongly prefer we design inside the envelope rather than plan for\nan uplift we may not get.\n\nTwo further points the committee asked me to pass on:\n\nThe programme must deliver measurable benefit within the first financial year.\nThe committee's patience for multi-year payback on digital projects is thin at\nthe moment.\n\nLicence and vendor commitments must be structured so they can be exited within\ntwelve months. We have been burned on a five-year contract before.\n\nI am copying Kenji so engineering has the number early. Kenji, if the\narchitecture you are designing cannot live inside $200k please tell me now and\nnot in December.\n\nBest,\nHelena\n\n--\nHelena Vosloo\nFinance Business Partner, Retail Technology\nMeridian Bank plc\n"
