    "content": "From: Nathan Cole <nathan.cole@meridianbank.example>\nTo: Daniel Okafor, Priya Raghavan <p.raghavan@northgate-advisory.example>\nCc: Helena Vosloo, Programme Mailbox\nDate: Thursday 6 August 2026, 16:05\nSubject: Broker channel - needs to be in release 1\n\nDaniel, Priya,\n\nI know discovery is nearly closed but this has come from the growth review on\nTuesday and it is not optional from a commercial standpoint.\n\nThirty-one per cent of our new current account volume last year came through\nintroducer relationships. If the new platform only serves direct applicants we\nwill be running two origination systems for another eighteen months, and the\nbroker experience stays on the 2014 stack.\n\nSo: the onboarding platform must also support broker-introduced applications in\nrelease 1.\n\nPractically that means a few things.\n\nThe system must allow an authorised broker to submit an application on behalf of\na customer. The system must provide a partner dashboard where a broker can see\nthe status of every application they have introduced. The system must calculate\nand record introducer commission against each activated account.\n\nI appreciate the baseline was signed on 24 July and this lands after it. I am\nhappy to take it through change control, but I want it understood that the\ncommercial case for the programme was built assuming broker volume, so treating\nit as a phase 2 item undermines the benefit numbers Helena is holding us to.\n\nCan we discuss on Monday.\n\nNathan\n\n--\nNathan Cole\nDirector, Intermediary Distribution\nMeridian Bank plc\n"
