    "content": "From: Daniel Okafor <daniel.okafor@meridianbank.example>\nTo: Programme Distribution\nDate: Tuesday 11 August 2026, 11:20\nSubject: Go-live date confirmed\n\nAll,\n\nThe steering committee has confirmed the date. The platform must go live on 2\nMarch 2027. This is now a board-level commitment and it has been communicated to\nthe group executive.\n\nBuild starts 1 September. That gives us six months.\n\nDaniel\n\n---\n\nFrom: Sofia Lindqvist <sofia.lindqvist@meridianbank.example>\nTo: Daniel Okafor, Programme Distribution\nDate: Tuesday 11 August 2026, 14:47\nSubject: RE: Go-live date confirmed\n\nDaniel,\n\nI need to raise a sequencing problem rather than object to the date itself.\n\nRegulatory sign-off for a new onboarding channel requires a 12-week observation\nperiod, which must commence after user acceptance testing completes and must run\non production-equivalent data. That is the standard the Financial Crime Committee\napplied to the digital savings launch and I have no basis to ask for a shorter\none here.\n\nIf UAT completes at the end of January, twelve weeks of observation takes us into\nlate April. I do not see how 2 March works unless UAT completes in early\nDecember, which would mean build finishing in about ten weeks.\n\nI am not trying to be difficult. I would rather we have this conversation in\nAugust than in February.\n\nSofia\n\n---\n\nFrom: Daniel Okafor <daniel.okafor@meridianbank.example>\nTo: Sofia Lindqvist, Programme Distribution\nDate: Tuesday 11 August 2026, 16:02\nSubject: RE: RE: Go-live date confirmed\n\nSofia,\n\nUnderstood. Let me take this back to steering. In the meantime the date stands as\nthe planning assumption and the team should work to it.\n\nDaniel\n"
