    "content": "# Discovery Wrap-up - Open Items Sweep\n\nDate: 14 August 2026. Open floor session. Attendance not formally recorded.\n\nThe purpose of the session was to sweep up anything raised during discovery that\nhad not landed in a workshop. Items below were called out from the floor. Where\nthe notes do not name a requester, the transcription did not capture who was\nspeaking.\n\n## Items raised\n\n- The system must provide a manual override for relationship managers so a\n  priority customer can be progressed ahead of the queue.\n\n- The system must support a paper application path for customers who cannot\n  complete the journey digitally.\n\n- The platform must integrate with the branch appointment booking system so a\n  failed digital verification can be converted into a branch appointment in one\n  step.\n\n- The system should retain the applicant's uploaded documents so they do not\n  have to be re-uploaded if the application is reopened.\n\n- The system must produce a monthly management information pack covering\n  application volume, conversion, abandonment stage and average time to\n  activation.\n\n- Somebody asked whether we are handling joint applications. No decision taken.\n  Carried as an open question.\n\n## Facilitator note\n\nSeveral of these items arrived without an identified owner. Priya flagged in the\nroom that items without a named business owner cannot be taken into build,\nbecause there is nobody to sign off the acceptance criteria. The manual override\nitem in particular was raised twice in discovery and has still not been claimed by\na named individual.\n\n## Next steps\n\nRequirements register to be finalised and issued for sign-off by 21 August 2026.\n"
